ons", "contents": [{"type": "text", "content": "Instructions: Complete the following steps. Fill in the Self Assessment."}]}]}], "type": "scholar", "_data": [{"type": "lab_options", "contents": [{"type": "has_nav", "content": true}, {"type": "has_exercise_controls", "content": true}]}], "id": 0, "stimuli": [{"type": "welcome", "template_override": 1, "_data": [], "id": 0, "contents": [{}]}, {"contents": [{"type": "slideshow", "value": {"coverimg": "engenn9le18ob03re2img01.jpg", "audiosrc": "engenn9le18ob03re2aud01", "images": [{"time": "0", "image": "engenn9le18ob03re2img01.jpg", "text": "", "id": 0}, {"time": "100", "image": "engenn9le18ob03re2img01.jpg", "text": "<span class= \"strong\"> Peter</span>: Ok Vanessa. Who was your best friend when you were growing up?<br />\n<span class= \"strong\"> Vanessa</span>: Honestly, I got along best with my cousin Cindy. We were very close. <br />\n<span class= \"strong\">Peter</span>: Are you guys still really tight knit? <br />\n<span class= \"strong\">Vanessa</span>: I talk to her once a week; either by phone or on social media. In fact, she told me that next week we will have been friends for over 25 years.<br />\n<span class= \"strong\">Sally</span>: That is adorable. What a cool milestone.<br />", "id": 1}, {"time": "26000", "image": "engenn9le18ob03re2img02.jpg", "text": "<span class= \"strong\">Vanessa</span>: Yeah, we are getting together next month. I'm really looking forward to it. At this time, next month we will be laughing and giggling like we were 12-year-old girls again. We are going to have so much fun together!<br />\n<span class= \"strong\">Sally</span>: Quiet Peter!<br />\n<span class= \"strong\">Peter</span>: I didn't say anything!<br />\n<span class= \"strong\">Sally</span>: You were about to. It was a preemptive strike.<br />\n<span class= \"strong\">Peter</span>: Nice. So V. What will you do on Sunday?<br />", "id": 2}, {"time": "51000", "image": "engenn9le18ob03re2img05.jpg", "text": "<span class= \"strong\">Vanessa</span> : Well, the event kicks off at 1:00 p.m sharp so we will need to get there a little early. At 10:30, Sally will be finishing up her chores, so you guys should come by the restaurant for brunch and then we can head over to the event from there.<br />\n<span class= \"strong\">Sally</span>: That sounds perfect.<br />\n<span class= \"strong\">Vanessa</span>:  Hopefully by then we will have gotten two more people to be on our team.<br />\n<span class= \"strong\">Sally</span>: Right. The mystery partners have yet to be revealed.<br />\n<span class= \"strong\">Vanessa</span>: Any suggestions?<br />\n<span class= \"strong\">Peter</span>: How about lumberjacks? What? I hear they're ok!<br />", "id": 3}]}}], "template_override": 1, "title": "", "type": "audio", "id": 1, "_data": []}]}], "_data": [{"type": "metadata", "contents": [{"type": "lesson_name", "content": "Like a House on Fire"}, {"type": "unit_name", "content": "Always Together"}, {"type": "position", "content": 3}, {"type": "origin", "content": "stub"}, {"type": "lesson", "content": 18}, {"type": "level", "content": "B2.1"}]}, {"type": "achievment_test", "contents": [{"type": "test", "content": "false"}]}, {"type": "objectives", "contents": [{"type": "primary", "content": "Describe situations in spoken interactions according to work and social contexts."}, {"type": "secondary_1", "content": " Understands general and detailed information as well as attitude and intention on a wide range of general and work topics, in conversations or presentations, spoken at a natural speed and in circumstances that make it more difficult to hear. "}, {"type": "secondary_2", "content": "Understands general and detailed information as well as attitude and intention on a wide range of general and work topics, in conversations or presentations, spoken at a natural speed and in circumstances that make it more difficult to hear. "}, {"type": "secondary_3", "content": " Understands general and detailed information as well as attitude and intention on a wide range of general and work topics, in conversations or presentations, spoken at a natural speed and in circumstances that make it more difficult to hear."}, {"type": "secondary_4", "content": "Understands general and detailed information as well as attitude and intention on a wide range of general and work topics, in conversations or presentations, spoken at a natural speed and in circumstances that make it more difficult to hear."}, {"type": "secondary_5", "content": "Understands specific information in written texts about the different social and work contexts."}, {"type": "secondary_6", "content": "Understands specific information in written texts about the different social and work contexts."}, {"type": "secondary_7", "content": "Understands specific information in written texts about the different social and work contexts."}, {"type": "secondary_8", "content": "Understands specific information in written texts about the different social and work contexts."}]}, {"type": "background_image", "content": "engenn9le18ob03re1img01.jpg"}, {"type": "learning_points", "contents": [{"type": "heading", "content": " The Future Continuous and Future Perfect Tenses"}, {"type": "describer", "content": " "}, {"type": "text", "content": "You use the <span class=\"underline\">Future Continuous </span> tense to talk about something happening at a particular time in the future. <br> When you use the <span class=\"underline\">Future Continuous</span>, the action will have started before that moment but it will not have finished at that moment."}, {"type": "text", "content": "For example:"}, {"type": "text", "content": "<span class=\"italic\">I <span class=\"strong\">will be sleeping</span> at 8 p.m. tonight. </span>"}, {"type": "text", "content": "The person will start sleeping at some point in the future and be sleeping at 8 p.m. "}, {"type": "text", "content": "You use the <span class=\"underline\">Future Perfect</span> tense to talk about an action in the future before another action in the future. When you use the <span class=\"underline\">Future Perfect</span>, you can sometimes think of the Future Perfect tense like the Present Perfect tense, but instead of your viewpoint being in the present, it is in the future."}, {"type": "text", "content": "For example:"}, {"type": "text", "content": "<span class=\"italic\">You can pick me up at 5 p.m. <span class=\"strong\">I will have finished</span> my work by then.</span>"}, {"type": "text", "content": "Look at the chart for the structure of the Future Continuous and Future Perfect tenses:"}, {"type": "table", "content": "{\"rows\":3,\"columns\":3,\"cells\":[\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"Name\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"Structure\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\" Example\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"Future Continuous\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"will (not) + be + v-ing\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\" <span class=\\\"italic\\\">At this time, next month we <span class=\\\"strong\\\">will be laughing</span> and giggling like we were 12 year old girls again. </span>\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"Future Perfect\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\" will + have + past participle\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"<span class=\\\"italic\\\">Next week <span class=\\\"strong\\\">we will have been</span> friends for over 25 years.</span>\\\"}\"],\"styles\":\" intro_table_border\"}"}, {"type": "example", "content": "In fact, she told me that next week we will have been friends for over 25 years."}, {"type": "example", "content": "At this time, next month we will be laughing and giggling like we were 12-year-old girls again. "}, {"type": "example", "content": "At 10:30, Sally will be finishing up her chores."}, {"type": "example", "content": "Hopefully by then we will have gotten two more people to be on our team."}]}, {"type": "learning_points", "contents": [{"type": "heading", "content": "The Future"}, {"type": "describer", "content": " You can use four different tenses to talk about the future."}, {"type": "text", "content": "When you talk about a things that are not decided or when you make a decision at the moment of speaking for the future, you use the modal <span class=\"italic\">will</span>."}, {"type": "text", "content": "When you ask about intentions, you use <span class=\"italic\">be going to</span>."}, {"type": "text", "content": "When you talk about things that are arranged, on the agenda or booked for the future, you use the Present Continuous tense."}, {"type": "text", "content": "When you talk about schedules, you use the Simple Present. "}, {"type": "table", "content": "{\"rows\":4,\"columns\":2,\"cells\":[\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"<span class=\\\"strong\\\">Will\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"<span class=\\\"italic\\\">What will you do on Sunday?\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"<span class=\\\"strong\\\">Be going to\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"<span class=\\\"italic\\\">We are going to have so much fun together!\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"<span class=\\\"strong\\\">Present Continuous\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"<span class=\\\"italic\\\"> We are getting together next month.\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\" <span class=\\\"strong\\\">Simple Present\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\" <span class=\\\"italic\\\">The event kicks off at 1 p.m. sharp.\\\"}\"],\"styles\":\" intro_table_border\"}"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "to look forward to"}, {"type": "definition", "content": "to feel happy and excited about something that is going to happen"}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": "(expression)"}, {"type": "example", "content": "Example: We are getting together next month. I'm really looking forward to it."}, {"type": "audio", "content": "engenn9le18ob03aud01"}]}, {"type": "target_word_describer", "contents": [{"type": "text", "content": " These are words you hear when describing a friendship."}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "tight knit"}, {"type": "definition", "content": "people who know each other very well and support each other"}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": "(adjective)"}, {"type": "example", "content": "Example: Are you guys still really tight knit?"}, {"type": "audio", "content": "engenn9le18ob03aud02"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "milestone"}, {"type": "definition", "content": "an important point in the progress or development of something "}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": "(noun)"}, {"type": "example", "content": "Example: What a cool milestone."}, {"type": "audio", "content": "engenn9le18ob03aud03"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "to reveal "}, {"type": "definition", "content": "to make something or somebody known"}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": "(verb)"}, {"type": "example", "content": "Example: We're going to reveal the mystery partners next week."}, {"type": "audio", "content": "engenn9le18ob03aud04"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "lumberjack"}, {"type": "definition", "content": "a person whose job is to cut down trees for wood"}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": "(noun)"}, {"type": "example", "content": "Example: John works in the forest as a lumberjack."}, {"type": "audio", "content": "engenn9le18ob03aud05"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "to head over"}, {"type": "definition", "content": "to depart and move or travel toward a specific destination"}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": "(verb)"}, {"type": "example", "content": "Example: We can head over to the event from there."}, {"type": "audio", "content": "engenn9le18ob03aud06"}]}, {"type": "takeaway_extension", "contents": [{"type": "text", "content": "Brainstorm with a group all the qualities that make a good friend."}, {"type": "text", "content": "Then make a list of negative characteristics that people have."}, {"type": "text", "content": "Individually, draw a large circle."}, {"type": "text", "content": "Put three names in the circle and write one name outside the circle."}, {"type": "text", "content": "The three names inside are friends. Write 4 to 5 characteristics or qualities that keep them in your circle."}, {"type": "text", "content": "For the person outside of the circle write negative qualities or characteristics that they possess that keep them outside your circle."}, {"type": "text", "content": "Share with a partner and ask questions."}]}, {"type": "takeaway_assessment", "contents": [{"type": "text", "content": "I brainstorm vocabulary to help describe people."}, {"type": "text", "content": "I analyze friendships and reflect on why I am friends with certain people and not with others."}, {"type": "text", "content": "I share my thoughts and feelings with a partner about qualities and characteristics."}]}]}